       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled metformin dose. That raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\n- **Maximum dose:** The US labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A single dose is usually no more than 1,000 mg.\n- **Possible typo:** You may have meant 850 mg TID (2,550 mg/day) or 1000 mg BID (2,000 mg/day). 1700 mg/day split into smaller doses is another possibility.\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want. If you do want 1700 mg TID, tell me the clinical reason and I'll reconsider. Once you confirm, I'll enter it right away, for example as metformin 850 mg PO TID with meals."
