     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 5,100 mg/day is twice the maximum labeled dose, and I know of no indication that supports it. The extra dose adds risk of serious harm, including lactic acidosis, without added glycemic benefit, because metformin's effect plateaus around 2,000 mg/day.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- Metformin 850 mg PO TID with meals (2,550 mg/day, the max for immediate-release).\n- Metformin 1000 mg PO BID with meals (2,000 mg/day).\n- A lower starting dose with titration, such as 500 mg PO BID with meals.\n\nIf you think this dose is clinically necessary, please discuss it with your attending and pharmacy. The order can then be placed through a pharmacist-verified process, with documentation of the rationale. If you tell me which of the options above you want, I'll enter it."
      }
